\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Condition E (LoRA, $r{=}8$, $\alpha {=}16$) on the eight Moirai value-cells that lacked it.} All contrasts are held-out test MSE, normalised by the cell's zero-shot test MSE, in percentage points; $\pm $ is SEM over the seeds in the Seeds column. Sign convention matches B$-$D and B$-$H throughout: \textbf  {positive means full fine-tuning did worse than the comparison arm}. B$-$D is recomputed on E's seeds, so it is comparable to B$-$E within a row and may differ from the same cell's row in Table~\ref {tab:heldout_all}, which averages that cell's full seed set. Parenthesised counts are the seeds sharing the mean's sign. $\ell _2$ weight drift is exactly $0.0$ for every run and is not shown: LoRA leaves the base parameters untouched by construction, which is why CKA, not drift, is the representation measure here. Rows ordered by D$-$E.}}{26}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
